WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.426 --> 00:00:15.813
Patrick Lussier is the CEO of an integrated wellness group.

2
00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:19.241
He is a war veteran with a new mission:

3
00:00:19.744 --> 00:00:22.979
helping communities become self-sustaining

4
00:00:23.335 --> 00:00:25.442
through For Better Community.

5
00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.374
Maryse Lehoux is a CPA and the group's Chief Financial Officer.

6
00:00:30.776 --> 00:00:34.193
She chose to build a career devoted to wellness.

7
00:00:34.709 --> 00:00:40.194
A yoga specialist, she and Patrick run their businesses

8
00:00:40.404 --> 00:00:43.205
and coach people who need it.

9
00:00:44.628 --> 00:00:47.861
For Better Community is a nonprofit organization

10
00:00:48.028 --> 00:00:52.579
working to empower the communities most in need.

11
00:00:53.594 --> 00:00:57.216
Our goal is to help them reach self-sufficiency

12
00:00:57.383 --> 00:01:01.259
and environmental sustainability through cooperation,

13
00:01:01.645 --> 00:01:05.839
empowerment, and the skills and tools required

14
00:01:06.176 --> 00:01:09.156
for long-term success.

15
00:01:10.719 --> 00:01:14.439
The philosophy of For Better Community is work in return.

16
00:01:15.342 --> 00:01:19.122
Every time residents receive support, they do a piece of work

17
00:01:19.289 --> 00:01:21.232
that gives something back to the community,

18
00:01:21.876 --> 00:01:25.050
so that it never feels like a handout, but like something

19
00:01:25.217 --> 00:01:27.187
they earned through their own effort.

20
00:01:29.368 --> 00:01:32.986
The Santa Cruz project aims to make the community

21
00:01:33.153 --> 00:01:35.058
of Santa Cruz self-sustaining.

22
00:01:35.955 --> 00:01:40.034
For Better Community would walk alongside it for five years,

23
00:01:41.221 --> 00:01:44.917
during which we expected to eliminate extreme poverty,

24
00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:48.114
bring the poverty rate down to 10 percent,

25
00:01:49.062 --> 00:01:52.149
and create direct employment by forming

26
00:01:52.316 --> 00:01:57.269
an agro-industrial cooperative, supported by specialists and technicians

27
00:01:57.436 --> 00:02:01.096
who would prepare the community to take over

28
00:02:01.263 --> 00:02:02.946
at the end of those five years.

29
00:02:04.672 --> 00:02:09.754
It also meant facing climate change without depending on the rainy season,

30
00:02:09.921 --> 00:02:12.274
through water projects.

31
00:02:15.723 --> 00:02:20.803
The first step is to acquire land for the community, large enough

32
00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.028
to hold the following areas.

33
00:02:24.646 --> 00:02:28.744
Water reservoirs built on the high ground of the site.

34
00:02:30.562 --> 00:02:35.092
The reservoirs feed lined ponds used to raise tilapia.

35
00:02:37.263 --> 00:02:40.374
Those ponds serve in turn as the base

36
00:02:40.541 --> 00:02:44.571
for growing vegetables vertically, through hydroponics.

37
00:02:45.596 --> 00:02:48.698
There is also space for raising cattle,

38
00:02:48.865 --> 00:02:50.987
pigs and poultry.

39
00:02:51.827 --> 00:02:53.645
Another project is beekeeping.

40
00:02:54.412 --> 00:02:58.036
The intent is to preserve the wooded part of the land

41
00:02:58.283 --> 00:03:02.021
and meet our environmental sustainability goal.

42
00:03:02.998 --> 00:03:07.724
Supporting the Álvaro Contreras school so it can restore its growing areas,

43
00:03:08.145 --> 00:03:11.772
with the food going to school meals for preschool,

44
00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:13.151
primary and secondary students.

45
00:03:15.457 --> 00:03:19.347
The project is not limited to economic development.

46
00:03:20.064 --> 00:03:23.558
Support for education would be continuous.

47
00:03:24.437 --> 00:03:29.298
At the preschool level, providing children with materials

48
00:03:29.465 --> 00:03:32.027
so they can enter the education system.

49
00:03:32.851 --> 00:03:36.198
At the primary level, with educational materials.

50
00:03:36.907 --> 00:03:39.927
And at the secondary level, by creating

51
00:03:40.094 --> 00:03:43.130
a trade school and directing secondary students

52
00:03:43.297 --> 00:03:46.784
toward the administration of the cooperative's activities,

53
00:03:46.951 --> 00:03:51.049
so they contribute to the development of their own community.

54
00:03:51.942 --> 00:03:55.481
Support for women and young mothers would be central,

55
00:03:55.982 --> 00:03:58.206
including support for the secondary school.

56
00:03:59.928 --> 00:04:02.919
Empowering women is a major axis

57
00:04:03.478 --> 00:04:04.960
of the project.

58
00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:12.574
That is why we would place emphasis on training people in personal finance,

59
00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:16.810
so they learn to manage their money and know how to invest it.

60
00:04:17.584 --> 00:04:21.376
Support for preventive health care is another important axis.

61
00:04:22.832 --> 00:04:24.106
For Better Community.

62
00:04:24.545 --> 00:04:25.961
Together we can.
